caption: Campaign Configuration
rule: campaign-configuration

Before play, the GM records the following campaign choices:

The Drive-source categories used by the campaign.

The number of active Drives taken from each source, from one to five.

The campaign's ordered Campaign Drives, if any.

The eligibility rules for selecting each source or Secondary Choice.

The maximum number of active sources permitted within each source category.

Which Drives require Secondary Choices and the legal options for those choices.

Whether each source category or Secondary Choice may be changed voluntarily.

The Mark or narrative requirements for an allowed change.

Whether Old Marks are archived in one universal field or separately by source.

The campaign's Mark Value.

Starting Character Value.

Prestige Reset Value, if Prestige is used.

Whether the optional Isekai Prestige module is used and which Prestige settings apply.

How fractional character-point progress is displayed.

Any campaign ruling about one event satisfying several Drives.

All characters in the same campaign should normally use the same campaign settings. Character-specific exceptions require an explicit subsystem rather than an unannounced sheet exception.
